The mass $m$ of a metal sphere is given by the expression $$m = \frac{\pi d^3 \rho}{6}$$ where $\rho$ is the density of the metal and $d$ is the diameter of the sphere.

Data for the density and the mass are given in Fig. 1.1.

{{figure:figure_1_1}}

